              "summary": "**Analyzing mirror reflections**\n\nThis left-right labeling can be quite tricky. When a person faces a mirror and raises their right hand, it appears to the observer as the left hand due to spatial interpretation. So, when they raise their right hand, it reflects on the left side from their perspective in the mirror. Also, I remember that a mirror preserves size and count, so a reflected image maintains the same angular size. It's all fascinating how mirrors can play with our perception of left and right!",
